# Artifact Collection
## i. Purpose
After acquiring the evidence, I moved to collecting relevant Windows artifacts for the investigation.

## ii. Tool Used
i. KAPE
ii. Windows forensic image/evidence
iii. KAPE output directory

## iii. Collection
I used KAPE to collect relevant Windows artifacts from the acquired evidence.
The collected artifacts included registry hives, event logs, Prefetch and other Windows artifacts that could help with reconstructing the activity on the system.

## iv. Artifacts Collected
i. SAM
ii. SOFTWARE
iii. NTUSER.dat
iv. ShellBags
v. Prefetch
vi. Windows Event Logs

## v. Output
The collected artifacts were saved in the KAPE output directory and were later used for Registry, event log and other forensic analysis.

## vi. Next Step
The collected artifacts were examined to identify user activity, persistence and other evidence related to the incident.
